      "The Brihadaranyaka Upanishad: Aham Brahmasmi — I am Brahman. This is not arrogance — it is the most humble statement possible. The ego says 'I am great.' The sage says 'I am not the ego at all.' What remains when the ego is dissolved is not nothing — it is everything. Brahman. The great sage Yajnavalkya teaches: Brahman is 'neti, neti' — not this, not this. It cannot be described in any positive terms because every description limits it. It is the witness behind all witnesses. The light by which you see all other lights — but which you cannot see directly, because you cannot see the eye with the eye.",
